29
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:55.000
There are three common ways to get a new
version of Windows Server.

30
00:01:55.250 --> 00:02:00.450
A clean install puts a fresh copy on a new
or wiped disk.

31
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.900
An in-place upgrade installs the new
version over the old one and keeps

32
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.750
settings, roles and data.

33
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Windows Server 2025 can upgrade from 2012
R2 or later.

34
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:17.850
A migration moves roles and data from an
old server to a new one.

35
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:23.300
Our lab VMs are blank, so there is nothing
to upgrade or migrate.

36
00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:27.550
A clean install also gives everyone the
same starting point.

37
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.800
