67
00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:30.100
On a blank disk you see one line: Disk 0
Unallocated Space.

68
00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.550
Unallocated means the disk has no
partitions yet.

69
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.800
Select it and select Next.

70
00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:41.250
You do not create or format anything,
because setup does that for you.

71
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:46.700
Load driver is only for storage
controllers that setup cannot see, and our

72
00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.950
