73
00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.600
On Ready to install, select Install.

74
00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.850
Setup copies files and asks nothing more
until the password.

75
00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.300
So what does setup create on that space?

76
00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.750
On a UEFI computer, you get four
partitions.

77
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:08.600
The EFI system partition is small and uses
FAT32, and the firmware starts Windows

78
00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.050
from it.

79
00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:15.500
The Microsoft reserved partition, or MSR,
is 16 megabytes and holds no data.

80
00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:19.350
The Windows partition uses NTFS and
becomes drive C.

81
00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.400
The Recovery partition holds the recovery
tools.

82
00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.450
In PowerShell, Get-Partition shows the
same list.

83
00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:30.900
Only the Windows partition gets a drive
letter, so leave the others alone.

84
00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:34.350
After the restarts, Desktop Experience
shows Customize settings.

85
00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.600
The user name is already Administrator,
the built-in admin account.

86
00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.650
Type the password twice and select Finish.

87
00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:46.300
Setup requires a complex password:
characters from three of four groups,

88
